{
  "dom_id": "step-11675",
  "name": "Example: \n                    Finding the Tangent or Cotangent of a Negative Special Angle",
  "problem": "Determine the value of $\\tan\\left(-\\dfrac{7\\pi}{4}\\right).$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we find an angle that's coterminal with $-\\dfrac {7\\pi}{4}$ that lies in the range $[0,2\\pi).$\n\n$$\n-\\dfrac{7\\pi} 4 + 2\\pi = \\dfrac{\\pi}{4}\\quad{\\color{green}{\\checkmark}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\tan\\left(-\\dfrac{7\\pi} 4\\right) = \\tan \\left(\\dfrac{\\pi} {4}\\right).$\n\nLet's remind ourselves of the special trigonometric ratios, as given by the unit circle.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14254214/assets/dbf36192ac332dc49ed75278838e989a37ac7d888311be1b8b059a7b59667aa6.png)\n\nFrom the unit circle, we see that the angle $\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}$ corresponds to the point $\\left( \\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}, \\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\right).$\n\n- Since the cosine of the angle corresponds to the $x$-coordinate, we have $\\cos \\left( \\dfrac{\\pi}{4}\\right) = \\dfrac{\\sqrt 2}{2}.$\n\n- Since the sine of the angle corresponds to the $y$-coordinate, we have $\\sin  \\left( \\dfrac{\\pi}{4}\\right)  = \\dfrac{\\sqrt 2}{2}.$\n\nTherefore, using the fact that $\\tan\\theta = \\dfrac{\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(-\\frac{7\\pi }{4}) & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})}{(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
  "html": "<div id=\"step-11675\" class=\"step\" style=\"display: block\" stepid=\"11675\" steptype=\"example\" contentid=\"3494\">\n            <div class=\"stepHeader\">\n                <div class=\"stepName\">\n                    Example: \n                    <a id=\"stepAnchor-11675\" class=\"stepAnchor\" style=\"font-weight: normal;\" name=\"step-8\">Finding the Tangent or Cotangent of a Negative Special Angle</a> \n                </div>      \n                <div class=\"helpButton\" stepid=\"11675\">?</div>\n            </div>\n            \n            <div class=\"exampleQuestion\">\n                <style type=\"text/css\">\n                            .mjpage .MJX-monospace {\n                            font-family: monospace\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage .MJX-sans-serif {\n                            font-family: sans-serif\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage {\n                            display: inline;\n                            font-style: normal;\n                            font-weight: normal;\n                            line-height: normal;\n                            font-size: 100%;\n                            font-size-adjust: none;\n                            text-indent: 0;\n                            text-align: left;\n                            text-transform: none;\n                            letter-spacing: normal;\n                            word-spacing: normal;\n                            word-wrap: normal;\n                            white-space: nowrap;\n                            float: none;\n                            direction: ltr;\n                            max-width: none;\n                            max-height: none;\n                            min-width: 0;\n                            min-height: 0;\n                            border: 0;\n                            padding: 0;\n                            margin: 0\n       